        <ArticleTitle>Triple inhaled therapy and mortality in moderate COPD: a randomised controlled trial</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND">Evidence on mortality benefit of triple therapy in moderate COPD is limited.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="FINDINGS">Among 4,800 participants, triple therapy reduced all-cause mortality compared with dual therapy over 52 weeks.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
